.TH CORTEX 1 "February 2026" "Cortex AI 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cortex \- persistent semantic memory for AI coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cortex
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Cortex AI
is a CLI tool that provides persistent memory for AI coding agents.
It uses vector embeddings via Ollama for semantic search and stores memories
locally using Gob encoding. This enables AI agents to store, retrieve, and
search memories using semantic similarity.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create
Create a new memory with title, type, and content.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-title " " \fIstring\fR
Memory title (required)
.TP
.BI \-\-type " " \fItype\fR
Memory types (repeatable or comma-separated): solution, issue, analysis, rule, any (required)
.TP
.BI \-\-content " " \fIstring\fR
Memory content (required)
.TP
.BI \-\-tags " " \fItags\fR
Memory tags (repeatable or comma-separated)
.TP
.BI \-\-output " " \fIformat\fR
Output format: text, json (default: text)
.RE
.TP
.B search \fIquery\fR
Search memories semantically by meaning.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-top " " \fIint\fR
Top K results (default: 5)
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-score " " \fIfloat\fR
Minimum similarity score 0-1 (default: 0.5)
.TP
.BI \-\-type " " \fItype\fR
Filter by memory type
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B list
List all memories with optional filtering.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-type " " \fItype\fR
Filter by memory type
.TP
.B \-\-include\-obsolete
Include soft-deleted memories
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B delete \fIid\fR
Permanently delete a memory by ID.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-obsolete
Delete all obsolete memories
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Skip confirmation prompt
.RE
.TP
.B export [\fIid\fR]
Export memories to JSON (default) or Markdown files.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Output directory or file path
.TP
.B \-\-all
Export all memories
.TP
.BI \-\-intent " " \fIstring\fR
Export a synthesis based on semantic search
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIformat\fR
Export format: json, markdown (default: json)
.RE
.TP
.B import \fIfiles...\fR
Import memories from JSON or Markdown files.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite existing memories
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Validate without importing
.TP
.BI \-\-output " " \fIformat\fR
Output format: text, json (default: text)
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIformat\fR
File format: json, markdown (auto-detected if omitted)
.RE
.TP
.B config
View and manage configuration.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-output " " \fIformat\fR
Output format: yaml, json, text (default: yaml)
.TP
.B init
Create default configuration file
.TP
.B path
Show configuration file path
.TP
.BI "get " \fIkey\fR
Get a configuration value
.TP
.BI "schema " \fItype\fR
Show or export JSON schema for templates
.TP
.BI "schema " \fItype\fR " \-o " \fIfile\fR
Export schema to file
.TP
.BI "template validate " \fIfile\fR
Validate a custom template file
.RE
.TP
.B start\-mcp\-server
Start the MCP (Model Context Protocol) server.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-transport " " \fItransport\fR
Transport mode: stdio, sse (default: stdio)
.TP
.BI \-\-address " " \fIaddr\fR
Server address for SSE transport (default: :8080)
.RE
.TP
.B completion \fIshell\fR
Generate shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell.
.TP
.B stats
Display database metrics and storage statistics.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B install\-man
Install the cortex man page to the system.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " " \fIpath\fR
Custom man page directory
.TP
.B \-\-system
Install to /usr/local/share/man (requires sudo)
.RE
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Path to configuration file
.TP
.BI \-\-storage " " \fIbackend\fR
Storage backend: gob, sqlite (default: gob)
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .ai/cortex/config.yaml
Project-local configuration file
.TP
.I .ai/cortex/cortex.gob
Single mode storage file (all memories + index)
.TP
.I .ai/cortex/memories/
Multi mode storage directory (individual memory files)
.TP
.I .ai/cortex/memories/index.gob
Multi mode index file
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CORTEX_BASE_PATH
Override the base storage path
.TP
.B CORTEX_STORAGE_BACKEND
Storage backend (gob)
.TP
.B CORTEX_STORAGE_PATH
Storage directory path
.TP
.B CORTEX_STORAGE_MODE
Storage mode (single, multi)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER
Embeddings provider (ollama)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL
Ollama model name (default: nomic-embed-text)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS_ENDPOINT
Ollama API endpoint (default: http://localhost:11434)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS_TIMEOUT
Ollama request timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B CORTEX_SEARCH_TOP_K
Default number of search results (default: 5)
.TP
.B CORTEX_SEARCH_MIN_SCORE
Default minimum similarity score (default: 0.5)
.TP
.B CORTEX_SEARCH_INCLUDE_OBSOLETE
Include obsolete memories in search (default: false)
.TP
.B CORTEX_OUTPUT_FORMAT
Default output format: text, json (default: text)
.TP
.B CORTEX_OUTPUT_COLORS
Enable colored output (default: true)
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a memory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex create \-\-title "JWT Fix" \-\-type solution \\
  \-\-content "Use refresh tokens for better security"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search memories semantically:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex search "authentication issues" \-\-top 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
List all memories:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex list \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export all memories to Markdown:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex export \-\-all \-\-format markdown \-\-output ./memories/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start MCP server for AI agent integration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex start\-mcp\-server \-\-transport stdio
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show database stats as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex stats \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate shell completions (bash):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex completion bash >> ~/.bashrc
.fi
.RE
.SH MEMORY TYPES
.TP
.B solution
Solutions to problems, fixes, and workarounds
.TP
.B issue
Known issues, bugs, and problems
.TP
.B analysis
Analysis of code, architecture, or behavior
.TP
.B rule
Project rules, conventions, and best practices
.TP
.B any
General-purpose memory type
.SH MCP INTEGRATION
The MCP server exposes the following tools for AI agents:
.TP
.B cortex_search
Semantic search for memories
.TP
.B cortex_create
Create new memories
.TP
.B cortex_list
List memories with filtering
.TP
.B cortex_get
Get a specific memory by ID
.PP
The MCP server uses JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio or SSE transport.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ollama (1)
.PP
Online documentation: https://github.com/cortex-ai/cortex-ai
